</blockquote>
<p>I'll switch around the description of the properties, that might help</p>
<blockquote>
<p>You've already introduced the -A's as &quot;families of three to five (each referred to as Group A through E)&quot;, which is confusing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You are finding a lot of important problems.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;The cranium has been replaced with a fleshless skull, identified as Falco rusticolus, and both arms have wings extending from the Humerus. The plumage is also identifiable as that of Falco rusticolus.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Using part of this. I don't want to have to say Falco rusticolus more than twice, and I already mention earlier that it's part of the that bird's skeletal system.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also, it occurs to me that there's no reason for the Foundation to be treating this as one entity spread across multiple places. Why isn't it described as 10 identical entities, with increasing hostility, etc.? You could almost interpret this as literally just one entity that somehow follows Foundation personnel, teleports between floors or something, and gets more hostile the further down they are because reasons.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's a neat idea, but it conflicts with the original image and story I had for the article.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The description of how it kills people really isn't all that interesting, and may be a good place to cut a lot of wordiness. We can just sort of assume &quot;big freaky dead bird man kills dudes good&quot;, unless those descriptions are really important somehow.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Will edit.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This strikes me oddly. Why not just 'weeping'?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I never clarify if the thing is a man or not, it just uses a male body. Thought I would just leave in there to clarify.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also, if they can't get to floor 9, how do they get to floor 10?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The stairwell connecting all floors is like that of any other stairwell; stairs leading to each floor, with a doorway (like a hospital or an office building).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>apparatuses</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was unsure about this, since the definition of apparatus implies it refers to all technical equipment of one mechanism, which would be the bunker. I guess I'll change it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>all that other stuff</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yup, changed</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Honestly, I don't see how this pertains to Pitch Haven at all, and if any of those details link to it, I can't find the connection.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is because I decided to not use any of Fantem's characters, since I didn't want to mess with the plot he was developing. I am writing a tale to connect this article and 1530, as Ananias, Salix, and Willow were all Edenites. In fact, I didn't know Fantem was writing a canon using all his articles until he told me.</p>
<p>I appreciate the in depth review, you should do them more. :P</p>
